	<item>
		<title>ROH-AEW talent holding wrestling fundraiser show for alma mater</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:56:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Deonna Purrazzo]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ROH]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[wrestling fundraiser]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397205</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Deonna Purrazzo is set to return to her hometown for a special wrestling-centric fundraiser in support of her&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/">ROH-AEW talent holding wrestling fundraiser show for alma mater</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Deonna Purrazzo is set to return to her hometown for a special wrestling-centric fundraiser in support of her alma mater high school.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with <a href="https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/ring-of-honor-champ-deonna-purrazzo-bringing-wrestling-nj-town-raise-awareness-major-issue">Fox News OutKick</a>, the AEW talent talked about the upcoming JTown SmackDown, which will put a spotlight on the lack of funding for schools in the area:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;ve worked with the athletic director, Bill Koch, for the past few months, since earlier this year, really, when we were reconnected over the Highlands Impact Aid Now rally at Jefferson, where we&#8217;re trying to draw attention to the fact that the funding formula for schools in New Jersey, the S-2 funding formula is not fair.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It&#8217;s not equitable to the students of the Highlands and the Pinelands. And so that kind of was the precipice to JTown SmackDown. We were raising money for the athletic department and for the JTEF, the Jefferson Township Educational Fund, which is all going to the students.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Purrazzo, the reigning ROH Women&#8217;s Pure Champion, will team with husband Steve Maclin to take on VSK and Emily Jaye when JTown SmackDown emanates from Jefferson Township High School in Oak Ridge on Friday, November 13.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/">ROH-AEW talent holding wrestling fundraiser show for alma mater</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW Dynamite/Collision Results &#8211; 11/11/26 (Live 3-Hour Special: Go-Home Show For Full Gear, Title Match, More!)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:05:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW Collision Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW Dynamite Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/11/26 AEW Collision Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/11/26 AEW Dynamite Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Collision]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dynamite]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[HBO Max]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Salt Lake City]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TBS]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Utah]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[West Valley City]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397168</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW Dynamite/Collision ResultsNovember 11, 2026Maverick Center in West Valley City, (Salt Lake City) UtahResults by: Alex Kahrs and&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/">AEW Dynamite/Collision Results &#8211; 11/11/26 (Live 3-Hour Special: Go-Home Show For Full Gear, Title Match, More!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AEW Dynamite/Collision Results</strong><br><strong>November 11, 2026</strong><br><strong>Maverick Center in West Valley City, (Salt Lake City) Utah</strong><br><strong>Results by: Alex Kahrs and Jerome Wilen of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1256" height="313" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w.png" alt="" class="wp-image-397209" style="aspect-ratio:4.012898602651379;width:271px;height:auto" srcset="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w.png 1256w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-600x150.png 600w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-380x95.png 380w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-550x137.png 550w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-800x199.png 800w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-1160x289.png 1160w" sizes="(max-width: 1256px) 100vw, 1256px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary welcomes us to the show before running down the lineup for tonight and Full Gear. From there we go to a video package looking back at the highlights Blood and Guts last week. From Julia Hart submitting to end the women&#8217;s B&amp;G match to Cope being forced to surrender in the men&#8217;s match, only for Darby Allin to be shoved off the cage and through a stack of tables by Wardlow.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go to footage from after the show, where Will Ospreay breaks the silence by trying to understand why Cope would break the oath the squad made to not surrender or submit. He runs down Adam by noting the kids watching him in his shirt, and whether he thought Darby wouldn&#8217;t be thrown off the cage&#8211;but Cope interrupts by addressing his own past with injury, saying he didn&#8217;t want to see that for anyone else. He speaks on the injuries the rest of the squad has suffered, and was trying to keep them from having to retire. If they can&#8217;t understand that, maybe this isn&#8217;t the place for him. He storms off as we head back to ringside.</p>



<h3 id="will-ospreay-and-kyle-fletcher-go-face-to-face" class="wp-block-heading">Will Ospreay and Kyle Fletcher go Face-To-Face</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Don Callis accompanies Kyle Fletcher to the ring as commentary talks about his match for the AEW World Championship at Full Gear. Kyle gets a microphone, and out next is Will Ospreay to a big pop from the crowd. As the champ enters the ring to pose for the fans, Kyle says to cut the music. He&#8217;s not out here to listen to this BS. This gets boos and &#8220;Ospreay&#8221; chants from the fans.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The chants turn to &#8220;f&#8211;k Don Callis,&#8221; to which Kyle asks if they&#8217;re done. He turns his attention to Ospreay, saying it&#8217;s been two years since they had a face-to-face conversation and they&#8217;re well due another. He reminds us of when he shaved his head, saying so much has happened&#8230;as the crowd tells him &#8220;you look stupid.&#8221; Kyle disagrees, realizing this is not an argument worth having as he addresses what has happened to Ospreay in that same timeframe. He got married, he got neck surgery, he came back from neck surgery, and he won the AEW World Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This gets &#8220;he&#8217;s World Champion&#8221; chants, to which Fletcher congratulates the crowd on being observant before bringing up his own success in that timeframe. He wraps it up by giving Ospreay some respect and thanks. Ospreay is surprised by this, thanking Kyle and saying he&#8217;s kept his eye on him for two years&#8230;and he&#8217;s proud of Kyle. Fletcher said he is grateful for everything that&#8217;s happened since, and this is a point Kyle reiterates as he explains that he would do everything again if he could.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He comes back around to the neck injury that took Ospreay out for months&#8230;upset that Ospreay went after Jon Moxley when he came back, when it was Fletcher who dropped him on his neck over and over to take him out. He wants the credit he deserves.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay admits that it was Kyle who broke his neck, addressing the pain he went through before explaining that the roar of the crowd is what kept him going when he was basically wrestling with one arm. It&#8217;s a painkiller for him, bruv. He talks about the bit that Kyle cut off moments ago, saying it&#8217;s a call to arms like the Batsignal for him. He then reminds Fletcher that even with a broken neck he beat him twice&#8230;and now, fully healed, he is wrestling at a level nobody can replicated.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He talks about outlasting seven opponents in Clockwork Carnage, beating the ace of AEW, hit a Black Arrow when the world needed it most, and beat Kenny Omega for the World Title at All In. He directs the production truck to play a clip he sent in this morning, reminding us that the last two men to see him backstage before he went out where Fletcher and Davis. He asks Kyle to tell him what he was feeling in that moment. Fletcher starts to bring up Don Callis, but Ospreay says he doesn&#8217;t want to hear Don&#8217;s words, he wants Kyle&#8217;s answer. As this goes on, there is a fan yelling out that Fletcher felt jealous, while Ospreay thinks Fletcher and Davis wanted to go out there with him like old times.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Eventually, Fletcher confirms that one fan&#8217;s theory by telling the champ that he was jealous. He was jealous that the man he hated most was about to win the biggest prize&#8230;until he realized that he had a chance to be the one to take it all away. Ospreay doesn&#8217;t believe him, saying he thinks his old pals wanted to be at ringside just like he believes deep down Fletcher still loves him. Kyle claims he never loved Will, and that he and Davis saw the truth about Ospreay. Callum Newman recently saw it, and someday everyone Ospreay ever loved will see it&#8230;including Will&#8217;s wife and son, and if his son won&#8217;t see it on his own, Fletcher will be there to tell him what kind of man Ospreay really is.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay notes these will be his final comments and then he will see Fletcher on Saturday, giving his challenger credit for his success but saying the two men are not on equal footing. He talks about everything he&#8217;s done in this business, and how he will show Fletcher what he showed Moxley, because he is Will Ospreay, and he is on another&#8211;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher slaps the champ in the face, telling him to do something about it and show him that killer instinct. Instead, Will retrieves the mic and finishes his sentence with &#8220;level&#8221; before leaving the ring as his music plays. With that, we go to a video package hyping up a dream match for Full Gear, as Adam Copeland challenges Kazuchika Okada for the AEW International Championship!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, The New Level make their entrance for our opening contest. Brodido come out next, but Creed and Kofi go after them to get things underway!</p>



<h3 id="the-new-level-austin-creed-and-kofi-vs-brodido-bandido-and-brody-king" class="wp-block-heading">The New Level (Austin Creed and Kofi) vs. Brodido (Bandido and Brody King)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All four men go at it at ringside until Brody finally brings Creed to the ring for the opening bell to sound, but Creed gets King to the outside for a dive through the ropes. Bandido rushes into the ring for a tope of his own, but is followed up with a dive from the top turnbuckle by Kofi. He goes around the ring to grab a chair, and encourages Creed to grab a chair of his own as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Creed takes down Bandido in the ring but is quickly dropped by Brody, who takes a guillontine leg drop from Kofi. Bandido takes out Kofi, but is caught with a fisherman&#8217;s buster by Creed! The New Level stay on top of things until King sends them out of the ring&#8230;only to be sent into the ring steps for his troubles as the ref begins the count. They start to celebrate this until Bandido takes them out with a dive to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He goes after Creed, bringing him up the ramp as he calls to Brody to grab a table&#8230;but Kofi attacks him with a chair as we find out both teams have been counted out!</p>



<h3 id="match-results-in-a-double-count-out" class="wp-block-heading">Match results in a Double Count-Out</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This barely fazes Brody as he brings the table out, and all four men are going at it. Brody gets sent off the stage and through a table as Creed and Bandio brawl to the back. Security tries to hold back King from going after Kofi as we cut to a video package honoring veterans on this Veterans Day.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Which I will do as well. Happy Veterans Day, and to those who served, thank you for your service!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go to footage from after Blood and Guts last week, with WrathLander and the Brawling Birds having some words about what went down as they gear up for their Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Championship match at Full Gear this weekend.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Orange Cassidy makes his entrance for our next match. David Finlay makes his way out next as commentary talks about what happened to Juice Robinson last Saturday, and the bell rings to get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="everyone-banned-from-ringside-orange-cassidy-vs-david-finlay" class="wp-block-heading">Everyone Banned from Ringside: Orange Cassidy vs. David Finlay</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Orange shows he is the smartest wrestler alive as he leaves the ring, walking to the corner where David set down his shillelagh&#8230;and tucks it underneath the ring apron to get it out of play! The bell rings after Cassidy gets back in the ring, but Finlay starts to show he doesn&#8217;t need that weapon as he goes to work on the former International Champion before Cassidy rolls out of harm&#8217;s way with his hands in his pockets.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He comes back just as Finlay leaves the ring, playing a bit of possum with David to keep him off his game. This leads to both men out of the ring as Cassidy finally catches Finlay with a dive, bringing him back in the ring before climbing the top rope&#8230;before getting caught in midair by Finlay for a backbreaker, dropping Orange down hard as we go to an ad break!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Finlay continues to wear down Cassidy, who fires back with his hands in his pockets. Finlay starts to mock him for this before laying Cassidy out with a rolling elbow. Orange starts to counter a suplex, eventually turning it around for one of his own sending Finlay to the mat. He dodges David in the corner, slamming Finlay against the turnbuckle on two corners. Finlay blocks a DDT, but takes a Stundog Millionaire instead. This allows Cassidy to connect with a DDT before going up top&#8230;where Finlay catches him with a bite on the head to stop his momentum!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cassidy returns the favor before knocking Finlay down for a diving DDT to the canvas&#8230;but Finlay manages to roll out of harm&#8217;s way. He reaches under the ring, pulling out a chair to distract the ref so he can use his shillelagh to level Cassidy for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-david-finlay" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall: David Finlay</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The ref notices the shillelagh and has it out with Finlay, trying to figure out if he used it to secure the victory. Eventually, David&#8217;s arm is raised in victory when The Cut make their way to ringside, only to be cut off by The Conglomeration.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary hypes up the rest of the lineup for tonight before we go backstage, where we hear from Andrade El Idolo. He talks about losing the National Championship at Collision. He admits it was a setback but also points out that when one door closes, another opens. He looks to make history by becoming the first Latino AEW World Champion. This is a promise from Andrade El Idolo, the real Latino man.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tommaso Ciampa defends the National Title he won from El Idolo later tonight!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We cut to a video hyping up AEW Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite and Thanksgiving Collision on November 25 and 26, respectively.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Backstage, we hear from Stokely ahead of the deciding match in the Best of 5 Series between FTR and the Motor City Machine Guns. We learn that the winners of this series will face whoever leaves Full Gear as the World Tag Team Champions, with Stoke promising that FTR are going to win this series and go on to become four-time tag champions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Dr. Britt Baker accompanies Persephone to the ring for our next match. Gypsy Mac is already in the ring as this match gets underway!</p>



<h3 id="persephone-vs-gypsy-mac" class="wp-block-heading">Persephone vs. Gypsy Mac</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Persephone immediately goes to work on Mac, wearing her down before Mac starts to fight back from the corner&#8230;but a big lariat and a bigger powerbomb takes Mac out as Persephone gets the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-persephone" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall: Persephone</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Persephone leaves the ring to shout at commentary over her TBS Title being &#8220;stolen&#8221; by Queen Aminata, who defends it in a 3-Way Match later tonight. Backstage, we hear from Hangman Adam Page as he addresses the agreement for the World Trios Title rematch at Full Gear being Texas Death. Page talks about his history with Swerve Strickland and the fact Swerve demanded this match be Texas Death. He says that going into this match is going in not knowing if you walk back out again. This match is meant to be for the trios titles but Page knows this is about something more.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Page has resisted and told everyone else not to give into the demands by Swerve, but Hangman admits this is about something more than him. Brodido joins him as he says his partners want Texas Death&#8230;they need Texas Death. He will walk side by side with his brothers into the mouth of hell.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">King understands Adam&#8217;s hesitation, but he must know that for years hate was Brody&#8217;s worth. Bandido helped him learn a new path, but Texas Death will let him embrace his old self. In Texas Death, you may pray to God that you will survive&#8230;with Brody admitting he doesn&#8217;t believe in God, but he does believe in violence. Bandido tells New Level and Swerve Strickland to meet their fate at Full Gear.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, we head to ringside for our next match. FTR make their entrance first as commentary talks about how they tied up the series at Collision, and the importance of this deciding match in the Best of 5 Series. Out next are the Motor City Machine Guns, and we get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="match-5-of-best-of-five-series-series-tied-2-2-ftr-dax-harwood-and-cash-wheeler-vs-motor-city-machine-guns-alex-shelley-and-chris-sabin" class="wp-block-heading">Match 5 of Best of Five Series (Series Tied 2-2): FTR (Dax Harwood and Cash Wheeler) vs. Motor City Machine Guns (Alex Shelley and Chris Sabin)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We seem to start with Dax and Sabin until some issues arise between both teams. Instead, we get Shelley and Harwood starting off. Dax with a side headlock takedown before hitting the ropes, rolling up Shelley for a two count. Alex fires back to get Harwood in an armbar, but Dax is back up for a tag to Wheeler. Double-team from FTR to no avail as they get taken to the mat by Shelley, who wrenches the arm of Cash.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wheeler breaks free as things break down with all four men going at it on the outside as we go to break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wheeler has Shelley in the corner for some right hands, but is caught with a Flatliner into the turnbuckle. Dax with a tag to keep him from going for a tag of his own, only to be sent to the corner himself. Tag is made but with the ref distracted he calls it off, while Dax and Cash pull Shelley away for some more shots. Shelley fights them off and gets the tag to Sabin, who goes at it with Dax.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Blind tag by Wheeler, but FTR are taken down with a flurry of offense by Sabin. He sends Dax out before dropping Cash to the canvas for a nearfall. Wheeler starts to fight back as we get a dueling chant for both teams, and the fight makes it to the corner where Sabin is attacked with a right hand. Tag to Dax, but he gets caught with a cradle for two! The fight spills outside once more as Wheeler is stopped by Shelley from using a ring bell. Dax kicks out of a pin attempt, sending Sabin into a ring bell shot by Cash.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cover by Harwood as we get a ten minute announcement, but Sabin manages to kick out at the count of two as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Things break down as we see all four men at it in the ring, with Stoke attempting to help out only for Sabin and Wheeler to clear out of the ring. Backslide by Harwood only gets a nearfall. He fires away with some shots on Shelley, who lands some of his own in response.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a five minute warning as Sabin gets involved as well, with Wheeler looking for a rolling suplex only to be stopped by the Guns. They fire up on Harwood with a double-team and stop Stokely from getting involved. They drop Harwood with a double team neckbreaker for the cover, but Wheeler narrowly breaks it up to save the match!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Harwood turns things around as he catches Shelley with a pin. Stokely helps with some leverage, but Alex shoves Dax off to break the pin for himself. He stares down Stoke who backs off, and FTR hit a Shatter Machine for the cover&#8230;but Sabin breaks it up! Stoke gets on the apron for a distraction, but takes a Cradle Shock for his troubles. FTR with some stuffed piledrivers on Sabin and Shelley, but it&#8217;s not enough as Shelley kicks out at two to save the match once again.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Fight Forever&#8221; chants from the crowd with one minute remaining. Shelley drops down to stop a stuffed piledriver attempt. Thirty seconds as FTR struggle to set up the piledriver, and Shelley blocks a Shatter Machine. He kicks off Wheeler and finishes a sunset flip for the pin&#8230;and with seconds to go gets the win!</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-winning-the-series-3-2-motor-city-machine-guns" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall (winning the series 3-2): Motor City Machine Guns</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">MCMG celebrate the win as FTR stare them down, stunned by the result. We now know the Guns will face either the Young Bucks or Davis and Doyle after Full Gear, as we see FTR shaking hands with MCMG before leaving the ring. We take a look back at AEW&#8217;s history in Salt Lake City before looking ahead to Full Gear this weekend in Phoenix.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, &#8220;Speedball&#8221; Mike Bailey makes his entrance for our next match as he challenges for the AEW National Championship. Out next is the champion as Tommaso Ciampa makes his entrance, while we get a look at Ciampa winning the title at Collision just as the rain started coming down in Miami. With that, we get this title match underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-national-championship-tommaso-ciampa-defends-against-speedball-mike-bailey" class="wp-block-heading">AEW National Championship: Tommaso Ciampa defends against ‘Speedball’ Mike Bailey</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The two charge at each other before Ciampa fires off some strikes, only for Speedball to return the favor and send the champ (uh) to the corner. Tommaso responds by sending Bailey to the outside, declaring &#8220;Ciampa rules&#8221; before leaving the ring to bring Bailey back. Bailey dodges him and hits the ropes, dodging him again to send the champ to the floor with a sky twister press.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bailey brings Tommaso back into the ring, following him right back out for a kick to the chest. He brings Ciampa back in, but the champ catches him off the ropes before sending Bailey back out&#8230;and then into the ring steps, before reminding us that Ciampa Rules. He gives a couple fans a high five for agreeing, and we see Bailey is busted open as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa has his challenger back in the ring, but Bailey turns things around with a release German suplex. He goes to the nearest turnbuckle but out goes Ciampa, who cuts him off at the pass. They fight on the turnbuckle as Bailey tries to go for a sunset powerbomb onto the apron, but to no avail. He connects with a thrust kick instead, before Tommaso catches him with an Air Raid Crash on the hardest part of the ring!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He brings Speedball back in the ring, connecting with a Project Ciampa for the cover&#8230;but Bailey kicks out at two! Bailey drops to evade a running knee, but also seems to be out as the ref checks on him. Ciampa looks for a powerbomb, but Speedball is able to keep low to stop it. He fires back with a kick, sending the champ to the mat&#8230;but Ciampa counters a powerbomb to pin the challenger for a two count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He hits the ropes, but Speedball counters with a powerslam for a nearfall of his own! PK from Speedball is followed with a double knee, and Ciampa retreats to the corner to evade another kick before forcing Bailey to collide with the turnbuckle. The fight ends up on the apron once more, where Speedball connects with an Ultima Weapon. He heads up top but is intercepted by Tommaso&#8230;but stops a superplex to get the champ in a bad position! Not for long, however, as Ciampa bites his feet to stop the kicks before sending him into the turnbuckle. Bailey is back up and connects with an Ultima Weapon off the top, but Ciampa kicks out!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He escapes to the opposite corner, only to take a spinning kick by Speedball. Bailey continues the attack until Tommaso catches him with an avalanche Project Ciampa for a close nearfall&#8230;followed by a running knee for another close two count! Bailey takes out his mouthguard, throwing it at the champ&#8230;who responds with another running knee, this one keeping the challenger down for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-still-aew-national-champion-tommaso-ciampa" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and still AEW National Champion: Tommaso Ciampa</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa celebrates his win but the lights cut out&#8230;they come back on, but quickly drop again as we get a look at the metronome on the stage. Out comes Ilja Dragunov, clearly calling out his shot as he makes his entrance to a big pop from the crowd. He points to the metronome and conducts the crowd as he gets a good look at the champion before posing for the crowd.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa&#8217;s had enough of this, pulling Ilja down as the lights return to normal. We get a staredown leading to Dragunov pointing to the screen, which reveals that the two will face off for the National Championship at Full Gear! &#8220;A-E-Dub&#8221; chants from the crowd as Ciampa responds to all this with a middle finger before leaving the ring, allowing Dragunov to enjoy his music as the champ heads back up the ramp.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Up next is the Mixed Tag Match as this 3-hour show continues!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">(With that I make a &#8220;hot tag&#8221; to Jerome to cover the final hour of this Full Gear &#8220;go-home&#8221; show!)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is Jerome Wilen tagging in for Alex Kahrs. Some technical issues on HBO Max end, so I missed the ring entrances. </p>



<h3 id="mixed-tag-jay-white-and-mercedes-mone-vs-death-riders-jon-moxley-and-marina-shafir" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Mixed Tag:</strong> <strong>Jay White and Mercedes Moné vs. Death Riders (Jon Moxley and Marina Shafir)</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Starting the recap of the match in progress&#8230;White runs the ropes, but Mox knocks him out of the ring. White tags in Mone who jaws at Shafir. Mox tags her in, but Mone&#8217; in the ring is short lived, as she tags in White. Shafir stays in the ring and kicks White in the back of the leg. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The action spills on the outside.  Mox lays into White, as does Shafir on Mone.&#8217; Mox bites White in the forehead. Shafir slaps White, chops him then kicks him. Mone&#8217; comes in with a backstabber on Shafir. White picks up Shafir and drops her with a backbreaker. Mone&#8217; is tagged in. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, White jabs Shafir, as she fires back with a slap. Shafir tags in a fresh Jon Moxley. Both men hammer away at each other. Mox connects with a knee to the head of White and then rolls him up for a two count. Moxley drop kicks White out of the ring, then leaps through the ropes, landing on White. Mone&#8217; leaps through the ropes, taking down Mox on the floor. Mox and White are back in the ring. Mox drops White with a piledriver and covers him for a two count only. Mox applies the face lock, but Mone&#8217; breaks it up. Mone&#8217; jaws at Mox, as he grabs her for a death rider, but is chop blocked by White. Mone&#8217; comes off the top with a frog splash on Mox. White is tagged in. White goes for a blade runner, but Mox counters with a paraddigm shift. Marina is in, Mone&#8217; is in! Marina round kicks Mone/&#8217; White comes in and grabs Marina. She has White locked in with a sleeper, while Mone&#8217; has a grip on Mox&#8230;Mone&#8217; goes down, as Mox and Marina hit rapid fire strikes on White. White recovers and hits Marina with a blade runner. Mox applies a headlock on White, a Mone&#8217; low-blows him while the ref&#8217;s back is turned. Mox drops Marina, as Mox then hits White with a king kong lariat. Maria connects with a brutalizer on Mone&#8217; as Mox pulls White out of the ring. Mone&#8217; taps out!</p>



<h3 id="winners-by-submission-jon-moxley-and-marina-shafir" class="wp-block-heading">Winners by submission: Jon Moxley and Marina Shafir</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the match Mone&#8217;s hits Shafir from behind locking in the statement maker.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="899" height="314" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_collision_logo_2_by_hellmen45_dj8y2rj.png" alt="" class="wp-image-397277" style="aspect-ratio:2.8631686585287914;width:239px;height:auto" srcset="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_collision_logo_2_by_hellmen45_dj8y2rj.png 899w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_collision_logo_2_by_hellmen45_dj8y2rj-600x210.png 600w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_collision_logo_2_by_hellmen45_dj8y2rj-380x133.png 380w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_collision_logo_2_by_hellmen45_dj8y2rj-550x192.png 550w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_collision_logo_2_by_hellmen45_dj8y2rj-800x279.png 800w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 899px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We are now on Collision, The Cut hit the ring and take out Moxley.  Kyle O&#8217;Reilly and Roderick Strong walk out. A taped Orange Cassidy makes his way out from the crowd. He hits David Finlay, Clark Conners and Ace Austin with Orange Punches. Roderick Strong picks up Austin Gunn and hits a backbreaker. O&#8217;Reilly has the ankle lock on Colten Gunn, but he gets pulled out of the ring before too much damage. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cassidy and Mox shake hands. Mone&#8217; gets in a cheap shot on Marina who is on floor trying to get up. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go backstage with Triangle of Madness. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The music of Young Bucks hits, as they are out first, followed by Jungle Jack Perry. Next up, the Don Callis Family. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Young Bucks and Jungle Jack Perry vs. Don Callis Family (El Clon, Kevin Knight, and Brian Cage)</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, as Cage and Nick start things off. Cage tosses Nick over the ropes, but he lands on the apron. The Bucks double team Cage, then sends Knight to the outside. The Bucks double team Knight ass he gets back in the ring. Perry is tagged in. El Clon is in. He chopped by Perry. Clon comes back, trying to pin Perry. Perry hits a drop kick on Clon. Knight is tagged in. Clon and Knight send the Bucks to the floor. Cage is in, but Cage sends him to the outside. Perry leaps over the ropes, but is caught by Cage. Knight pulls up the ring apron, as Perry is under the ring. The Bucks hit Cage and Clon with superkicks. Knight is hit with a superkick. Perry and the Bucks run the ropes and take flight, landing on the Don Callis family on the floor. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Knight hits a leaping drop kick on Perry who was on the shoulders of Cage. Knight is hammer thrown into the ropes, as Perry hits Knight with a lariat. Perry tags in Nick Jackson, sending Knight to the floor. Nick takes out Cage with a superkick off the apron. The Bucks take out Knight, then El Clon, who then rolls to the floor. Knight is back in, as the Bucks German Suplex Knight, who rolls to the outside. Matt gets hung up on the ropes, and is grabbed by Cage, but Nick makes the save. Perry walks on the top of barricade, connecting with a leaping kick to the head on Cage. In the ring, Nick takes down Knight and El Clon&#8230;Nick is up on the ropes, as Knight takes him down. Perry comes in and hits Knight with a DDT. Cage grabs Perry as El Clon picks him up and drops him. Knight comes off the top with a UFO splash on Perry. El Clon covers him, but the Bucks break up the pin attempt. Matt takes Clon down with a superkick. The Bucks then superkick Cage and Knight. Nick is tagged in. Double piledriver on Clon and Knight. Cage is sent to the floor with knee strikes. The Bucks hit the BTE Trigger on Clon to get the pin.</p>



<h3 id="winners-by-pinfall-the-young-bucks-and-jack-perry" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Winners by pinfall: The Young Bucks and Jack Perry</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go backstage with Lexy Nair talking to Divine Dominion. They say they have become stronger after Blood and Guts. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-COMMERCIAL BREAK-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Lexy Nair is with the Bucks and Jack Perry. Perry says he is coming for his rematch against Samoa Joe. He then leaves. The Bucks says they are fighting champions. They say Davis and Doyle gave them the worst loss of their careers. They says they are the founding fathers of The Elite. They will still be four time AEW World Tag Team Champions after Full Gear.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back in the venue, the music of Wardlow hits, as he comes out with Davis and Doyle.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Wardlow vs. Nick Comorato</strong> </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Both men lock up. Nick puts Wardlow in a headlock, then tries to take him down with a shoulder tackle. Wardlow headbutts Nick. Wardlow lays out Nick with a big lariat. Wardlow grabs Nick and picks him up and connects with the powerbomb. He covers Nick for the pin.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-wardlow" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by pinfall: Wardlow</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the match, Griff Garrison and Aaron Solo come in to prevent Wardlow from powerbombing Nick, but are taken out by Davis and Doyle.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go backstage with Lexy Nair talking to Hyan and Maya World. Hyan says she and World celebrated one year in AEW, taking nothing for granted. Hyan says she is going to show everyone why she will be the next TBS Champion. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back in the venue, Blake Christian and Lee Johnson make their way to the ring. Next up are the champions, who make their way out and down to the ring. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>ROH World Tag Team Championship:</strong> <strong>Mistico and Mascara Dorada defends against The Swirl</strong> <strong>(Blake Christian and Lee Johnson)</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, as Blake and Mistico start off. We get no handshake. Mistico takes down Blake, but he is quick to get up to his feet. Johnson is tagged in.  Johnson refuses the handshake from Mistico. Johnson is sent to the floor and then leaps through the ropes, landing on Johnson. Mistico rolls Johnson back in the ring and tags in Dorada. Blake is tagged in. Mistico and Dorada double team Blake, sending him to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Dorada and Johnson collide. Mistico is tagged in. He comes off the ropes with a crossbody on Johnson. Mistico thrust kicks Johnson. He comes off the tope with a senton, landing on Johnson. Mistico covers Johnson, but Blake breaks up the pin attempt. Johnson connects with a destroyer on Mistico on the apron, as he rolls to the floor. Mistico is back in the ring, as Blake and Johnson double team him. Lee covers Mistico for a two count. Mistico tries to fight off Blake and Johnson. Dorado comes off the top with a big crossbody on Johnson. Dorado flies over the top, landing on Blake who is on the outside. Mistico rolls up Johnson to get the pin to retain.</p>



<h3 id="winners-by-pinfall-and-still-roh-world-tag-team-champions-mistico-and-darado" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Winners by pinfall and still ROH World Tag Team Champions: Mistico and Darado</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the match, Nick Wayne interrupts the celebration of the ROH World Tag Champions. He asked everyone if they heard the news&#8230;Nick Wayne is all over Utah. He says this morning he came back to dry land after his cruise this weekend, to tell everyone he beat Chris Jericho twice, as we get a pryo.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-COMMERCIAL BREAK-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, the challengers are introduced first. Skye Blue is out first. Hyan is out next. The champion is out last, making her way to the ring. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>3-Way Match for the TBS Championship:</strong> <strong>Queen Aminata (c) vs. Skye Blue vs. Hyan</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, as Hyan goes for a quick pin. Blue is sent to the floor. Hyan tries again for a quick pin on the champion, but only gets a two count. All three ladies are in the ring, as we get a short brawl. Hyan connects with a running knee strike on Aminata. Hyan connects with knee strikes on the champion and Blue. Hyan picks up Blue and sends her on top of Aminata. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h3 id="dynamite-quick-results" class="wp-block-heading">Dynamite Quick Results:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The New Level (Austin Creed and Kofi) vs. Brodido (Bandido and Brody King) ends in a Double Count-Out</li>



<li><strong>Everyone Banned from Ringside:</strong> David Finlay def. Orange Cassidy</li>



<li>Persephone def. Gypsy Mac</li>



<li><strong>Match 5 of Best of Five Series (MCMG Win 3-2):</strong> Motor City Machine Guns (Alex Shelley and Chris Sabin) def. FTR (Dax Harwood and Cash Wheeler)</li>



<li><strong>AEW National Championship:</strong> Tommaso Ciampa def. ‘Speedball’ Mike Bailey</li>



<li>Collision Quick Results:</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Mixed Tag:</strong> Death Riders (Jon Moxley and Marina Shafir) def. Jay White and Mercedes Moné </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Young Bucks and Jungle Jack Perry def. Don Callis Family (El Clon, Kevin Knight, and Brian Cage)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>ROH World Tag Team Championship:</strong> Mistico and Mascara Dorada def. The Swirl</p>



<h3 id="still-to-come" class="wp-block-heading">Still to Come:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Still to Come:</li>



<li><strong>3-Way Match for the TBS Championship:</strong> Queen Aminata (c) vs. Skye Blue vs. Hyan</li>
</ul>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/">AEW Dynamite/Collision Results &#8211; 11/11/26 (Live 3-Hour Special: Go-Home Show For Full Gear, Title Match, More!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Former WWE champion launching &#8216;Not Too Small&#8217; wrestler agency</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:56:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Misc. News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Chavo Guerrero]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[wrestling agency]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397202</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In an interview with Fightful, Chavo Guerrero Jr. gave details on the launch of Not Too Small, a&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/">Former WWE champion launching &#8216;Not Too Small&#8217; wrestler agency</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with <a href="https://www.fightful.com/wrestling/338615-chavo-guerrero-brad-small-agency/">Fightful</a>, Chavo Guerrero Jr. gave details on the launch of Not Too Small, a talent agency in partnership with longtime wrestling attorney Brad Small.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Guerrero, a former WWE Cruiserweight Champion who has since worked for the likes of TNA, Lucha Underground, AEW, and more, explained the history behind launching the agency, aiming to negotiate wrestling contracts and help wrestlers land deals in ventures outside pro wrestling itself:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brad Small, he’s been my lawyer/agent since 2003, doing most of my WWE/WWF stuff and of course, all my TNA and Lucha stuff. Definitely all of my Hollywood stuff. Brad’s just — he’s represented all the big players in the industry and we were talking, with his connections and my connections, why are we not representing wrestlers on our own and doing our own agency? That got us thinking, it was a little while back we started talking about that. He was all for it — I just think it’s such a great fit because what happens in this industry, you have people trying to represent wrestlers but first of all, if you don’t know wrestling contracts, they’re a whole different ball game. It’s an own set, it’s got its own place in contracts. Anybody from Hollywood trying to read a wrestling contract would be like, hell no, no way, don’t ever sign that. I’ve heard that time and time again from wrestlers trying to get a new guy doing their contacts, that’s just not how it works.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, you really have to know contracts. Brad Small knows contacts. Then, with all the Hollywood stuff that we’ve got going on, that I’ve got going on, people that’s he’s represented like Eva Longoria and Chris Jericho, man it was just like a perfect fit. So, we created our agency called Not Too Small, playing off his name and our Guerrero size. We’ve always been not too small, but we’re too small in a big man’s business [laughs].</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That’s what’s going on man, we created our own agency and we’re going to represent wrestlers not only in the wrestling world but also transitioning into the Hollywood world or in other business ventures like brand endorsements and really anything that they want to do to kind of make their brand bigger. There’s a couple of other people in that space, but I just feel that we really just have so much to offer. Talking to Tony Khan, right away he got back to us and was like, ‘Wow, this is really great.’ A couple other people from WWE got back to us and it was pretty cool to hear their feedback.</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe title="Chavo Guerrero Announces New Agency, Talks Maculay Culkin, Working With Spielberg, Lucha UG" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/NuRt44ygod4?start=1187&amp;feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/">Former WWE champion launching &#8216;Not Too Small&#8217; wrestler agency</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Ludwig Kaiser&#8217;s legal counsel files &#8220;Motion to Compel&#8221; to seek alleged victim’s medical records in battery case</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:46:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ludwig Kaiser]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Motion to Compel]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397193</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>According to a new report from F4WOnline, Ludwig Kaiser (real name Marcel Barthel) and his defense are still&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/">Ludwig Kaiser&#8217;s legal counsel files &#8220;Motion to Compel&#8221; to seek alleged victim’s medical records in battery case</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">According to a <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/ludwig-kaiser-files-motion-seeking-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">new report from F4WOnline</a>, Ludwig Kaiser (real name Marcel Barthel) and his defense are still making attempt to gain access to potentially important evidence in the ongoing battery case against the WWE/AAA talent.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report notes a “Motion to Compel” was filed on Tuesday, November 10 with Kaiser’s defense asking for the court to direct the Office of the State Attorney to hand over all medical records pertaining to the injuries suffered by Richard Reap, the alleged victim. It is further noted that within the filing, the defense for Kaiser argues that being able to review the medical records could show evidence Reap did not suffer the injuries he claims or that the injuries did happen, but are unrelated to the incident.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">F4WOnline further states that Assistant State Attorney Juanda Padgett <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/ludwig-kaisers-defense-given-access-to-medical-records/">initially agreed to share the medical records</a> with Kaiser’s defense back in late October. However, Padgett did not send the records due to Reap’s attorney due to objecting to the idea. Reap has hired his own legal counsel, potentially indicating he could be planning a civil case against Kaiser after the criminal matter is resolved. At the present time, Kaiser is facing a misdemeanor battery charge as a result of incident between himself and Reap which happened in and then just outside of an elevator at the apartment complex Kaiser was living in at the time in Orlando, Florida.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Another pre-trial conference is scheduled for December 17, with a possible trial that could take place January 4-22, 2027, if the case does not get extended or end in a plead agreement before those dates.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Reap has accused Kaiser of attacking him following the elevator stopping at Reap’s floor. Both Kaiser and Reap do agree the altercation took place after Reap had asked Kaiser and his girlfriend Andrea Bazarte to “please have some manners,” as they were getting overly affectionate with each other in the same elevator Reap was on. Kaiser claims Reap swore at him, the made a racist comment that involved contacting ICE on Bazarte. Kaiser has admitted to pushing Reap, but said that he only did it after Reap aggressively lunged towards him and then made threats – all while in the elevator.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The original arrest report notes local police viewed the surveillance video from inside the building and could see Kaiser punching and pushing Reap. The report also indicates that police did see a scratch on Reaps head.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kaiser entered a “not guilty” plea in response to the misdemeanor battery charge. Kaiser&#8217;s defense had  made attempts to get the case dismissed under Florida’s “Stand Your Ground” law, with the claim Kasier&#8217;s use of non-deadly force against Reap was justified in order to protect himself and Bazarte against “imminent use of unlawful force.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kaiser, under the El Grande Americano gimmick, is the current AAA Mega Champion. He won the title after defeating <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dominik_Mysterio">Dominik Mysterio</a> in a No Disqualification Match on the second night of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tripleman%C3%ADa_34">Triplemanía 34</a> back on September 13, 2026.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/">Ludwig Kaiser&#8217;s legal counsel files &#8220;Motion to Compel&#8221; to seek alleged victim’s medical records in battery case</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TKO employees reportedly frustrated over safety issues with UFC and WWE events in Saudi Arabia</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:42:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[employees]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[events]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TKO]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[UFC]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397190</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>According to a report from Ben Fowlkes of Uncrowned, TKO employees are reportedly frustrated with the parent company&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/">TKO employees reportedly frustrated over safety issues with UFC and WWE events in Saudi Arabia</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">According to a report from <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/mma/article/inside-tkos-saudi-arabia-crisis-ufc-wwe-workers-speak-out-as-safety-fears-escalate-everyone-just-cant-believe-this-020000151.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Ben Fowlkes of Uncrowned</a>, TKO employees are reportedly frustrated with the parent company of WWE and UFC moving forward with events in Saudi Arabia despite ongoing military conflict in the country. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fowlkes notes sources told Uncrowned that several of TKO&#8217;s employees have grown increasingly frustrated at the company&#8217;s insistence on going through with events in Riyadh even when missile and drone attacks by the Houthi militia in Yemen continue. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A recent attack happened in Riyadh&#8217;s financial district just hours after Saturday&#8217;s WWE Crown Jewel event ended. While it was confirmed in other reports that WWE Superstars left by the time a missile struck a tower owned by the state-run Aramco oil company on Sunday, some of TKO&#8217;s employees said they felt their safety has been little more than an afterthought.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source, speaking on the condition of anonymity due to fear of reprisal, told Uncrowned, &#8220;Why are you still even having these shows at this point?&#8221; I think the answer is, if they chose not to do the show, they would lose out on millions and millions of dollars.&#8221; The source continued on by saying, &#8220;If we don&#8217;t do the shows in Saudi Arabia or [United Arab Emirates] or Doha or wherever we are going, then our fourth-quarter earnings will be off and our shareholders aren&#8217;t going to get their money So it&#8217;s all about greed. They don&#8217;t care about anybody&#8217;s well-being. The level of greed with this company is so gross.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Uncrowned reached out to TKO representatives for comment regarding safety concerns expressed by its employees and the decision to move forward with events in Saudi Arabia. Uncrowned notes at the time of their report, TKO did not respond. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source inside TKO told Uncrowned, &#8220;All [TKO executives] talk about is if the State Department says it is OK to fly there. The rest of us are like, &#8216;If the State Department has to think about it at all, let&#8217;s just postpone.&#8217; That&#8217;s what all the other sports are doing. Why can&#8217;t TKO?&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ahead of a UFC Fight Night event planned to be held in Riyadh on December 5, some TKO employees told Uncrowned they are increasingly upset with what they see as a disregard for employee safety and a lack of communication about potential contingency plans.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Not one email has gone out saying, &#8216;Here are the details and the plans for December 5th.&#8217; That&#8217;s crazy,&#8221; said one source. &#8220;They don&#8217;t tell you anything. They just throw it at you. How about a backup plan? How about a safety letter? &#8216;Hey, if x happens, we go do y. We&#8217;ll all meet here. We&#8217;ll do this. We&#8217;ll do that.&#8217; Nothing.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Furthermore, now, with added concerns regarding the continued ongoing military conflict, some within TKO have stated that executive leadership is not taking their safety seriously enough.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source told Uncrowned, TKO does not care about about their employees and people within the company are tired of how they are being treated. &#8220;They don&#8217;t f&#8212;&#8211;g care about you one bit. People are just getting tired of the way they&#8217;re getting treated. They get treated like s&#8211; and everybody&#8217;s tired of it. The lack of communication, the greed, the lack of appreciation, people are just sick of it.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Other sources have told Uncrowned that events in Saudi Arabia and the risks that come with traveling and working from what is essentially an active conflict zone, have pushed some off TKO&#8217;s employees to their breaking point. One longtime TKO employee told Uncrowned the mood among staff had darkened after the company refused to move or postpone events even after airports had been attacked in Saudi Arabia. It was added that some of the employees under the TKO banner have said communication from top executives has been lacking, despite during a recent company town hall meeting, Mark Shapiro, TKO&#8217;s President and Chief Operating assured employees the company would &#8220;not hesitate&#8221; to cancel or postpone events in the region in the face of &#8220;danger or a further escalation&#8221; in the military conflict.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Also during the company town hall meeting, Shapiro acknowledged canceling the events in Saudi Arabia would impact business in &#8220;a very negative way,&#8221; but then said &#8220;business is secondary&#8221; to employee safety. However, Shapiro added TKO is currently on track for an lucrative year financially, which was noted in the company&#8217;s <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/mma/article/tko-reports-136-billion-in-q3-revenue-with-ufc-alone-pulling-in-5192-million-from-july-to-september-221454928.html">third-quarter earnings repor</a>t, which included an increased targeted revenue of $5.83 billion for the year.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source, speaking on the condition of anonymity, told Uncrowned, &#8220;Everyone is talking about the Middle East shows, Who has to go, who can get out of going. Some people say they are waiting until the time to fly comes and telling [executives] that they won&#8217;t go. But I don&#8217;t know how many will follow through with that. This is a company that can fire you for no reason or any reason. Everyone just can&#8217;t believe this is a choice that they are being forced to make — fly into a war zone or risk getting fired before Christmas.&#8221; Former and current employees described a company culture at that is shortsighted and focused on maximizing short-term profitability, with little regard for employees who keep the company going. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One source told Uncrowned, &#8220;We&#8217;ve come to the realization, this is what it is. We&#8217;re going to either have to accept it or leave, because nothing&#8217;s going to change at this point. But it&#8217;s time to get called out. People think it&#8217;s fine and you get taken care of. People realize the fighters get paid s&#8212;. I mean, that&#8217;s obvious. You guys have covered that aspect of it. People know, and the fighters are starting to speak up for themselves, but it doesn&#8217;t stop with them. That&#8217;s the message I want to get across. Everyone across the whole company gets treated like s&#8212;, whether you&#8217;re a fighter or a camera guy.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A report this past Tuesday from <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">F4WOnline</a> noted a match between Gunther and Finn Balor was ultimately dropped from Crown Jewel&#8217;s lineup because Gunther decided against traveling to Saudi Arabia. However it was also noted that Balor had reservations about making the trip, but the belief internally was that he would have traveled had Gunther agreed to participate.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/">TKO employees reportedly frustrated over safety issues with UFC and WWE events in Saudi Arabia</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
