			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Jim Herd, former WCW executive who fired Ric Flair, passed away last month at age 87</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397162-jim-herd-former-wcw-executive-who-fired-ric-flair-passed-away-last-month-at-age-87/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397162-jim-herd-former-wcw-executive-who-fired-ric-flair-passed-away-last-month-at-age-87/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:15:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Jim Herd]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[passed away]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WCW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397162</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In his column post on 11/10/26 for Uncrowned, Conrad Thompson revealed the sad news that Jim Herd, former&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397162-jim-herd-former-wcw-executive-who-fired-ric-flair-passed-away-last-month-at-age-87/">Jim Herd, former WCW executive who fired Ric Flair, passed away last month at age 87</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In his column post on 11/10/26 for <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/wrestling/article/jim-herd-former-wcw-boss-who-famously-fired-ric-flair-dies-at-87-wrestlemania-43-dates-saudi-arabia-211206092.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Uncrowned</a>, Conrad Thompson revealed the sad news that Jim Herd, former WCW executive passed away last month at the age of 87.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Herd was WCW&#8217;s first executive vice president after Ted Turner acquired the promotion from Jim Crockett. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Herd ran WCW from 1988 until he resigned in January 1992. Herd is best known for firing Ric Flair after a contract dispute in July 1991.  Herd wanted to repackage Flair, with him cutting his hair, wearing an earing and going by the name of “Spartacus.” Herd ended up firing while he was still the champion. Flair signed with the WWF and took the big gold belt with him. Managed by Bobby Heenan, Flair was billed as the “Real World Champion.” </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Left scrambling without a belt or champion, in which Flair was supposed to have defended at the 1991 Great American Bash against Barry Windham, WCW held a title match where a hell Lex Luger defeated Windham to win the vacant championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Flair returned to WCW in 1993.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gimmicks Herd was criticized for was Oz, The Ding Dongs, and The Hunchbacks. However, Thompson states Herd has not been given enough credit for characters such as Big Van Vader, the Great Muta, Scott Steiner and bringing Terry Funk. Furthermore, Herd was responsible for the feud and series of matches between Flair and Ricky Steamboat and putting the WCW World Championship on Sting. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thompson notes after leaving WCW, Herd worked in the casino business. Prior to his tenure in WCW, Herd was a regional manager for Pizza Hut.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WCW found its financial and ratings success during era under Eric Bischoff during the Monday Night War, beating WWF Raw in the television ratings for 83 week. However, after the WWF shifted to a more adult-oriented product, WCW began a downward spiral. After the AOL/Time Warner merger, hit with consistent financial losses and very poor ratings, AOL/Time Warner canceled WCW programming from TBS and TNT.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WCW aired for the final time on TNT on March 21, 2001, when it was announced by Vince McMahon in a live simulcast with WWF Raw on then TNN, he acquired the promotion for a reported $4.2 million which included the video library, trademarks and several contracted talent not under AOL/Time Warner deals.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wrestleview sends its condolences to the family and friends of Jim Herd.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397162-jim-herd-former-wcw-executive-who-fired-ric-flair-passed-away-last-month-at-age-87/">Jim Herd, former WCW executive who fired Ric Flair, passed away last month at age 87</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397162-jim-herd-former-wcw-executive-who-fired-ric-flair-passed-away-last-month-at-age-87/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Bret Hart: WCW &#8216;should be sued for unprofessional wrestling&#8217;</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397159-bret-hart-wcw-should-be-sued-for-unprofessional-wrestling/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397159-bret-hart-wcw-should-be-sued-for-unprofessional-wrestling/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:37:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bill Goldberg]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bret Hart]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WCW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE Hall of Fame]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397159</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In an interview with The Johnny I Pro Show, Bret Hart talked about his reputation as a safe&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397159-bret-hart-wcw-should-be-sued-for-unprofessional-wrestling/">Bret Hart: WCW &#8216;should be sued for unprofessional wrestling&#8217;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with The Johnny I Pro Show, Bret Hart talked about his reputation as a safe performer in the ring before bringing up Bill Goldberg.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The WWE Hall of Famer, who sustained an injury from a Goldberg kick at Starrcade 1999 that ultimately brought an end to his in-ring career, stated that the issues with Goldberg stemmed from WCW failing to communicate properly with their top star:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You’ve got to know what you’re doing when you go out there a little bit. It’s not like Goldberg — I won’t go on a big thing about Goldberg, but Goldberg just hurt me because he didn’t know how to do anything different. No one taught him, no one showed him, no one explained to him like Bill, it’s not really real. You can’t actually kick somebody in the head as hard as you can, you just can’t.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">No one took the time to tell him that in WCW, where it’s like, they should be sued for unprofessional wrestling, for putting me in the ring with a guy that didn’t know anything about wrestling.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hart has not been shy about his criticisms of Goldberg in the past, though his fellow former WCW Champion has apologized several times for the incident over the years.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Source: <a href="https://www.fightful.com/wrestling/bret-hart-wcw-shouldve-been-sued-for-putting-me-in-the-ring-with-goldberg/">Fightful</a></p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="BRET “HITMAN” HART - THE MAN BEHIND THE LEGEND" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/SJTVqKbHQUU?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397159-bret-hart-wcw-should-be-sued-for-unprofessional-wrestling/">Bret Hart: WCW &#8216;should be sued for unprofessional wrestling&#8217;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397159-bret-hart-wcw-should-be-sued-for-unprofessional-wrestling/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report: Member of The Vision remains in Saudi Arabia after sustaining injury at WWE Crown Jewel</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397154-report-member-of-the-vision-remains-in-saudi-arabia-after-sustaining-injury-at-wwe-crown-jewel/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397154-report-member-of-the-vision-remains-in-saudi-arabia-after-sustaining-injury-at-wwe-crown-jewel/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:01:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bronson Reed]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[hospital]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[injury]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397154</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Fightful Select reports WWE star Bronson Reed is reportedly still in Saudi Arabia after being legitimately injured at&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397154-report-member-of-the-vision-remains-in-saudi-arabia-after-sustaining-injury-at-wwe-crown-jewel/">Report: Member of The Vision remains in Saudi Arabia after sustaining injury at WWE Crown Jewel</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fightful Select reports WWE star Bronson Reed is reportedly still in Saudi Arabia after being legitimately injured at last Saturday&#8217;s Crown Jewel, after suffering rib and kidney injuries. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report also notes Reed did not legitimately travel back to the United States and that WWE assigned one of their teams medical personnel to stay with him and has their top international executive in the region that is onsite to ensure Reed receives VIP treatment. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Reed&#8217;s injury came after he was slammed off the stage by Oba Femi onto what was said to be production equipment. Reed came out during the WWE World Tag Team Championships Match in an attempt to keep the titles on his Vision stablemates Bron Breakker and Austin Theory who were defending the titles against Penta &amp; Je’Von Evans. However, Penta and Evans would go on to capture the titles. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Reed, after dropping weight, returned this past September after suffering torn biceps back on the February 23, 2026 episode of Raw.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Secondary source: <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/report-bronson-reed-still-in-saudi-arabia-after-wwe-crown-jewel-injury/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">F4WOnline</a></p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="Oba Femi DESTROYS The Vision to set up Penta and Je&amp;apos;Von Evans&amp;apos; win: WWE Crown Jewel 2026 highlights" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/hK-NxaMUBtg?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397154-report-member-of-the-vision-remains-in-saudi-arabia-after-sustaining-injury-at-wwe-crown-jewel/">Report: Member of The Vision remains in Saudi Arabia after sustaining injury at WWE Crown Jewel</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
